  "rationale": "The set does supply candidate causes/treatments (VC, life-science, industry sector) whose effect on regional location can be attributed, and these were surfaced from the company descriptions rather than copied from the query, which is positive. However, the causal design is weak: several columns (sector, VC, life-science) blur treatment and confounder roles, and the strongest 'confounders' (talent density, stage focus) are only loosely genuine common causes of BOTH a specific treatment and the outcome. proximity_cluster is effectively a restatement of the outcome (a near-collider/mediator on location) and should not be adjusted for. No clearly external common cause (e.g., real-estate cost, founder origin, incentives) was surfaced, so the confounder quality is modest."
